        "depth": 2,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "Split the sparse inclusion-exclusion reduction into four independent modulo accumulators. This removes the single loop-carried accumulation dependency across groups of predecessor obstacles, exposing legal instruction-level parallelism (and potential compiler scheduling/vectorization opportunities) while preserving the same modular sum.",
